41 ### SQ-02: Unknown Commit Outcome
45 | **Source** | `FINDINGS.md` §SQ-02; `PUBLICATION-ATOMICITY-REVIEW.md` §C4; Q3-QUAL-03 |
46 | **Requirement** | Distinguish confirmed failure, confirmed success, unknown native commit outcome |
47 | **Current evidence** | LatticeDB local store throws on failure or returns on success. No ambiguous state. Process crash during `txn.Commit()` → state either pre- or post-commit on reopen (WAL). Acknowledgment loss not distinguishable. N6 tests managed `before-commit` fault only. |
48 | **Stage 1 disposition** | **Qualified** — Explicit Stage 1 boundary. No false success/failure reporting in known paths. |
50 | **Rationale** | Stage 2 must not rely on an unqualified commit outcome model. The limitation must be explicitly acknowledged in Stage 2 publication paths. |
51 | **Required work** | 1. Document Stage 1 limitation in Stage 2 specification.<br>2. Stage 2 must define conservative behavior: on any persistence failure, replay prior accepted state; never claim success without verified commit.<br>3. If Stage 2 introduces multi-process or distributed publication, unknown-outcome reconciliation must be independently qualified. |
52 | **Evidence required** | Stage 2 specification includes explicit unknown-outcome section; Stage 2 qualification plan includes crash-recovery test (if applicable). |
54 | **Closure authority** | Stage 2 independent review + owner acceptance |
55 | **Blocking stage** | Stage 2 authorization |
59 ### SQ-03: Concurrency and Snapshot Semantics (Invariant 10)
63 | **Source** | `FINDINGS.md` §SQ-03; `D4-CONCURRENCY-REVIEW.md` §H2; Q3-QUAL-03 |
64 | **Requirement** | Query behavior during concurrent publication follows a defined snapshot or freshness contract |
65 | **Current evidence** | `_writeGate` (SemaphoreSlim) serializes ALL reads and writes. Queries block during publication. No MVCC, no snapshot isolation. Freshness re-check only via caller-provided `ExpectedPublication`. No concurrent stress test. |
66 | **Stage 1 disposition** | **Qualified** — Serialization is the demonstrated model. Not snapshot isolation. Acknowledged Stage 1 boundary. |
68 | **Rationale** | Stage 2 must not assume snapshot isolation. The current serialization model must be explicitly documented as the Stage 1 contract. Stage 2 may propose a stronger contract but must independently qualify it. |
69 | **Required work** | 1. Document current contract: "Queries serialize behind publication; observe either prior or new complete state; no partial/intermediate visibility."<br>2. Stage 2 specification must either (a) accept serialization as the concurrency model with explicit qualification, or (b) define and implement a stronger contract (e.g., publication versioning with non-blocking reads) with independent evidence.<br>3. If (b), Stage 2 must include concurrent stress test with measurable isolation level. |
70 | **Evidence required** | Stage 2 concurrency model documented; independent qualification of chosen model. |
72 | **Closure authority** | Stage 2 independent review + owner acceptance |
73 | **Blocking stage** | Stage 2 authorization |
83 | **Current evidence** | Refusal tested by tampering fresh stores (version 99, missing meta, namespace mismatch). No historical fixture generated. D5 accepts no migration. |
