99 - **Concurrent publication snapshot contract** (invariant 10): query behaviour during concurrent publication follows a defined snapshot or freshness contract.
103 - **Validation**: pre-commit validation failures leave durable state unchanged.
104 - **Commit**: `txn.Commit()` is the durability point; atomic all-or-nothing.
105 - **Supersession**: newer generation wins; stale publication rejected; no generation regression.
106 - **Reopen**: ordinary reopen (no rebuild) and full rebuild/reopen produce equivalent query results.
107 - **Recovery**: unknown-outcome quarantine, corroboration by reopen, no blind retry.
108 - **Native concurrency/republication**: concurrent writers serialized by file lock; first writer commits; others fail/wait; durable state consistent; no mixed-state exposure.
